schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Layer 2 fee reduction vs. Ethereum Mainnet throughput limit
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Ethereum Mainnet handles roughly 15-30 transactions per second; a simple
    transfer costing several dollars on Mainnet often costs less than a cent
    on a Layer 2, and a 500-member community token system could cost
    "hundreds of dollars" per month on Mainnet versus "less than a dollar
    per month" on Base or Arbitrum.
  evidence: >-
    Asserted directly in the article's body text (no external citation or
    dataset linked); the article's own references section links to Ethereum's
    documentation on Layer 2s and L2BEAT for independent verification, but no
    specific figure is sourced to either.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/layer-2s.md
  interpretation: >-
    Directionally reliable (L2 fees are genuinely orders of magnitude lower
    than Mainnet during congestion) but the specific numbers (15-30 tps,
    "hundreds of dollars," "less than a dollar") are illustrative estimates,
    not measured figures with a timestamp — gas prices and L2 fees both
    fluctuate significantly with network conditions.
  uncertainty: >-
    High for the exact dollar figures (unsourced, likely to drift with
    market conditions); moderate-low for the qualitative claim that L2s are
    meaningfully cheaper, which is well-established.
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/layer-2s.md
    transformation: quoted
    authorship: ai-assisted
